{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_y6zzaedl324aak3khl4ebylk5bvndiuoinpglow7ixwlrcmwm2ua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The C-to-Rust translation is complete:\n\n**Summary:**\n\nI implemented a C-to-Rust translation of the `emlang` interpreter, an esoteric stack-based programming language. The implementation includes:\n\n1. **`utils.rs`** — A simple `strcpy_to_heap` helper that returns an owned `String`.\n\n2. **`data.rs`** — `Data`, `DataType`, and `DataValue` types with `Display` impls and constructors for int/string values.\n\n3. **`em.rs`** — The instruction (`Em`) types, with `Display` for both `EmType` and `Em`, and a growable `Program` collection.\n\n4. **`stack.rs`** — A safe Rust `Stack` with push, pop, dup, swap, shrink_to, clear, and gc operations. Memory management is handled by Rust's ownership system (no manual `free`).\n\n5. **`env.rs`** — The interpreter environment with the `run` loop dispatching on `EmType`. I had to use `Box::leak` to provide a placeholder `Program` reference at construction time, since the `Env` struct holds a borrow that's set during `run`. The `run` method works on a local clone to avoid the lifetime constraint issue.\n\n6. **`parser.rs`** — Tokenizer and parser implementing the same character-by-character algorithm: handles quotes with escape sequences, plain tokens (keywords, ints, comments via `:x`, special tokens like `:3`, `;3`, etc.), and a cross-reference pass that links `IfBegin`/`IfEnd`, `LoopBegin`/`LoopEnd`, and `PrintBegin`/`PrintEnd`.\n\n7. **`lib.rs`** and **`interfaces/main.rs`** — Provide `parse` and `usage` matching the original C `main.c` semantics.\n\nI also created a `resources/test` symlink to `resources/tests` to match the path expected by `tests.rs`.\n\nAll 9 test programs (comments, comparisons, count_to_10, error, hello_world, if, math, negative_nums, runtime_error) execute correctly, with `runtime_error.eml` correctly producing an error and the others succeeding."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":69229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c02d8ef3-7e64-4fff-84d3-dd76965f7cce","uuid":"0b8b3153-b23f-4d79-95d7-4f370fe7706a"}
